TI  - Anesthetic Management of Acute Right Tension Pneumothorax in a Child With Left 
      Main Bronchial Foreign Body: A Case Report.
PG  - e72639
LID - 10.1002/ccr3.72639 [doi]
LID - e72639
AB  - In children with complete unilateral main bronchial obstruction from foreign body 
      aspiration, positive pressure ventilation may overdistend the contralateral 
      ventilated lung, leading to barotrauma and tension pneumothorax. Sudden hypoxemia 
      and hypotension should prompt rapid clinical assessment, including lung 
      ultrasound, and immediate decompression.
