TI  - When Foreign Body Aspiration Is Not the Whole Story: Reconsidering Imaging 
      Escalation in Infants With Apparent Tension Pneumothorax.
PG  - e72805
LID - 10.1002/ccr3.72805 [doi]
LID - e72805
AB  - In infants with suspected foreign body aspiration and radiographic tension 
      pneumothorax, failure to improve after appropriate decompression should prompt 
      immediate diagnostic reconsideration. Early CT or advanced imaging may identify 
      congenital lung anomalies such as CPAM, particularly when positive-pressure 
      ventilation creates misleading radiographic findings.
