TI  - Bilioptysis as a Diagnostic Cornerstone for Occult Bronchobiliary Fistula.
PG  - 100627
LID - 10.1016/j.opresp.2026.100627 [doi]
LID - 100627
AB  - Bilioptysis is a rare clinical entity characterized by the expectoration of 
      biliary secretions through the respiratory tract. Its presence is pathognomonic 
      of a biliopulmonary or bronchobiliary fistula. We present the case of a 
      69-year-old man with a history of ileal carcinoid tumor with metastatic liver 
      disease, who underwent hepatectomy and had a history of abdominal biliary 
      collections. The patient was admitted for bibasal cavitary pneumonia associated 
      with acute respiratory failure. During the clinical course, the patient developed 
      bilioptysis, whose final diagnosis could be confirmed by imaging and 
      bronchoscopic studies. The etiopathogenesis, differential diagnosis, and 
      therapeutic options of this rare complication are discussed.
