AB  - A bronchoscopy is an essential tool for clinicians and health care providers 
      treating patients with lung diseases. Since its introduction to clinical practice 
      by Shigeto Ikeda in 1966, flexible bronchoscopy has become an essential tool in 
      the diagnosis and management of patients with lung diseases. Rigid bronchoscopy 
      can be particularly helpful in therapeutic cases.
