COIS- Declarations. Ethics approval and consent to participate: All porcine lungs used 
      in this study were obtained from a licensed slaughterhouse, where the animals 
      underwent standard veterinary inspection and were handled in accordance with 
      hygiene protocols for fresh meat. The storage, transport, handling, and disposal 
      of these animal by-products were conducted in compliance with national 
      regulations and were registered with the competent veterinary authority. All 
      procedures complied to relevant German legislation, and the pigs were humanely 
      euthanized at the slaughterhouse by the approved captive bolt pistol. Experiments 
      performed on the right lungs from the IPF and RA-associated UIP-pattern fibrosis 
      patients, who had undergone lung transplantation, were approved by the local 
      ethics committee of Hannover Medical School (ethics approval number: 10194 BO K 
      2022). Written informed consent was obtained from these human research 
      participants included in the study. Consent for publication: By providing written 
      informed consent to take part in the study, participants consented to anonymized 
      results being published. Competing interests: The authors declare no competing 
      interests.
