TI  - [Endotracheal mantle cell lymphoma: a case report].
PG  - 1178-1181
LID - 10.3760/cma.j.cn112147-20250617-00337 [doi]
AB  - Mantle cell lymphoma (MCL) is a subtype of B-cell non-Hodgkin lymphoma, typically 
      diagnosed at an advanced stage with frequent extranodal involvement. Common sites 
      of infiltration include the gastrointestinal tract, eye, liver, spleen, bone 
      marrow, and central nervous system; however, pulmonary involvement-particularly 
      tracheobronchial manifestation-is exceedingly rare. We report the case of a 
      60-year-old woman presenting with a 4-month history of cough and progressive 
      dyspnea. Chest CT revealed a polypoid mass arising from the left tracheal wall, 
      causing significant luminal narrowing. Under general anesthesia, bronchoscopic 
      biopsy and tumor resection were performed, with histopathological examination 
      confirming MCL.
