TI  - [Pulmonary Wedge Resection for a Dental Instrument Retained in the Bronchus for a 
      Long Time Period:Report of a Case].
PG  - 1059-1062
AB  - It is often difficult to remove long-standing foreign bodies by bronchoscopy. The 
      patient was a 57-year-old woman who accidentally aspirated a dental instrument 
      during dental treatment. Two years later, an abnormal shadow was noted on chest 
      imaging, and she was referred to our hospital. Chest computed tomography (CT) 
      revealed a 2-cm foreign body in the left lower lobe. Bronchoscopy was performed, 
      but the foreign body could not be removed. Thoracoscopic partial resection of the 
      left lower lobe was undertaken for removal of the foreign body.
