TI  - A Case of Cryobiopsy of a Large Allergic Bronchopulmonary 
      Aspergillosis-Associated Mucus Plug.
PG  - e70221
LID - 10.1002/rcr2.70221 [doi]
LID - e70221
AB  - A 68-year-old woman presented with cough and dyspnoea. She was diagnosed with 
      allergic bronchopulmonary aspergillosis with mucus plugs. Forceps biopsy failed 
      to remove a large plug, but cryobiopsy with a 2.4 mm cryoprobe was successful. 
      This case demonstrates that even large mucus plugs can be removed by cryobiopsy.
