TI  - Preoperative Rehearsal in the Removal of an Airway Foreign Body in a Preterm 
      Septic Neonate.
PG  - 8812622
LID - 10.1155/crot/8812622 [doi]
LID - 8812622
AB  - We report a case of a septic, 21 day old, former 26-week neonate who had clinical 
      and x-ray concern for an airway foreign body. 3D CT remodeling was used to 
      identify the foreign body as the tip of a suction catheter. Preoperative planning 
      to confirm optimal bronchoscopic instrumentation was done, and the foreign body 
      was successfully removed in a single attempt. This case highlights the importance 
      of preoperative radiographic evaluation and instrument rehearsal in high-risk 
      airway foreign body cases.
