TI  - An insight into interventional bronchoscopy.
PG  - 100321
LID - S1470-2118(25)00039-9 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.clinme.2025.100321 [doi]
LID - 100321
AB  - The emergent field of interventional bronchoscopy provides an alternative 
      approach for the diagnosis and management of a range of respiratory conditions. 
      Within malignant disease, robotic navigational bronchoscopy provides a stable 
      platform to sample small and difficult to reach pulmonary nodules, while 
      malignant central airway obstruction can be managed through transcopic stent 
      insertion. A range of therapeutic modalities have been developed for benign 
      disease, which provide alternatives to standard therapy, particularly in the 
      context of endobronchial valves for chronic obstructive pulmonary disease, and 
      bronchial thermoplasty for asthma, while transbronchial cryoexcision lung biopsy 
      offers a non-surgical option for undiagnosed interstitial lung disease. With a 
      rich pipeline of technology being developed through robust clinical trial 
      processes, the field of interventional bronchoscopy will continue to grow to 
      become an invaluable asset, not only to the field of respiratory medicine, but to 
      the general physician.
