TI  - Lipoid proteinosis, a rare cause of eyelid margin lesions.
PG  - 104210
LID - S1091-8531(25)00108-9 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.jaapos.2025.104210 [doi]
AB  - Lipoid proteinosis is an extremely rare multisystemic disorder characterized by 
      the deposition of collagenous hyaline-like material in various tissues, including 
      the eyelid margins. We present the case of a 7-year-old boy who had twice 
      undergone diagnostic laryngoscopy, bronchoscopy, and biopsy. This case emphasizes 
      the role of ophthalmologists in detecting rare systemic disorders and the value 
      of collaboration in optimizing patient care outcomes, particularly in the context 
      of rare and complex medical conditions.
