TI  - Cryoextraction of Subacute, Adhesive and Immobile Airway Blood Clot With Short 
      Freezing Time: A Case Report.
PG  - e70155
LID - 10.1002/rcr2.70155 [doi]
LID - e70155
AB  - We report a rare case of a patient experiencing persistent exertional dyspnoea 
      due to a subacute, adhesive and immobile airway blood clot following haemoptysis. 
      Cryoextraction with short freezing times, which fragmented the 
      clot into small pieces, proved effective, despite previous reports on acute 
      airway blood clots recommending longer freezing times.
