OAB - Lung cancer screening (LCS) has been implemented or is in the process of being 
      introduced in several countries worldwide as a strategy to detect lung cancer at 
      an earlier stage, potentially allowing a curable therapeutic approach [1, 2]. 
      Virtual navigation bronchoscopy (VBN) is gaining attention among the available 
      diagnostic tools for evaluating peripheral pulmonary lesions due to its potential 
      to enhance diagnostic accuracy [3]. However, LCS often detects incidental 
      findings that require follow-up imaging, typically using low-dose computed 
      tomography (LDCT) [4].
