TI  - A Case of Prostate Cancer Recurrence Presenting With Lung Cancer-Like Computed 
      Tomography Findings.
PG  - e70568
LID - 10.1002/rcr2.70568 [doi]
LID - e70568
AB  - A 58-year-old man had undergone surgery for prostate cancer 2 years previously. 
      He was admitted to the respiratory department because of a solitary nodule in the 
      right lung. He underwent bronchoscopy and was diagnosed with prostate cancer 
      recurrence. This case highlights the importance of active bronchoscopy.
