DP  - 2026 Mar 13
TI  - A case report of inflammatory myofibroblastic tumor resection via fiberoptic 
      bronchoscopy with literature review.
LID - 10.1186/s12887-026-06631-x [doi]
LID - 356
AB  - Inflammatory myofibroblastic tumor (IMT) is a relatively rare pediatric neoplasm 
      that usually presents as a solitary pulmonary lesion and may lead to both 
      intrapulmonary and extrapulmonary complications. Although surgical resection 
      remains the standard treatment, endoscopic resection via fiberoptic bronchoscopy 
      has been rarely reported. We describe the case of a 7-year-old boy admitted for 
      recurrent cough. Imaging revealed pulmonary atelectasis, and the tumor was 
      successfully resected using snare electrocautery during fiberoptic bronchoscopy. 
      No recurrence was observed during follow-up. This case suggests that 
      bronchoscopic resection may represent a viable alternative treatment for selected 
      cases of IMT.
