TI  - Hemoptysis With Expulsion of Coil Fragments in a Patient With Aorto-Bronchial 
      Fistula of the Thoracic Descending Aorta.
PG  - e71276
LID - 10.1002/ccr3.71276 [doi]
LID - e71276
AB  - Massive hemoptysis following TEVAR, especially in patients with prior coil 
      embolization, should raise immediate suspicion for aortobronchial fistula. This 
      rare but life-threatening condition demands prompt imaging, bronchoscopy, and 
      often urgent surgical repair. Early multidisciplinary collaboration significantly 
      improves prognosis.
