TI  - Subglottic Stenosis After COVID-19 Mimicking Bronchial Asthma, Treated by 
      Bronchoscopic Resection.
PG  - e70377
LID - 10.1002/rcr2.70377 [doi]
LID - e70377
AB  - A woman developed dyspnea following COVID-19 without prior intubation. The 
      patient was initially treated for asthma; however, her symptoms persisted. 
      Evaluation revealed subglottic stenosis due to a membranous structure. 
      Bronchoscopic resection and balloon dilation resulted in symptomatic improvement. 
      This is the first reported case of membranous subglottic stenosis following 
      COVID-19.
