TI  - Successful Closure of Postoperative Bronchopleural Fistula With Granulation After 
      Submucosal Injection and Spreading of Fibrin Glue.
PG  - e71103
LID - 10.1002/ccr3.71103 [doi]
LID - e71103
AB  - In the treatment of bronchopleural fistulas, it is necessary to consider 
      bronchoscopic intervention and surgery depending on the patient's condition and 
      fistula size. Submucosal injection and spreading of fibrin glue under 
      bronchoscopy may be useful methods for the closure of small, pinhole-like 
      fistulas that are several millimeters in size.
