DP  - 2025 Sep 22
TI  - Robotic-assisted bronchial reimplantation for post-tuberculosis bronchial 
      stenosis: surgical technique.
LID - 10.1510/mmcts.2025.035 [doi]
AB  - This report presents a novel robotic-assisted surgical technique for bronchial 
      reimplantation in patients with complete bronchial stenosis after tuberculosis 
      treatment. A 34-year-old female patient with progressive dyspnoea was diagnosed 
      with complete bronchial stenosis and total left lung atelectasis. After 
      unsuccessful bronchial dilation attempts, robotic-assisted bronchial 
      reimplantation with veno-venous extracorporeal membrane oxygenation support was 
      undertaken. Intra-operative bronchoscopy ensured airway patency throughout the 
      procedure. At 1-year follow-up, the patient remained asymptomatic in daily 
      activities, with no late complications or restenosis, reinforcing the long-term 
      efficacy of the procedure. This technique demonstrates the potential for enhanced 
      surgical outcomes in managing complex bronchial stenosis. The findings highlight 
      the viability of this advanced technique in improving respiratory function and 
      patient recovery.
