TI  - Accidental Spectacle Handle Aspiration During Tracheostomy Care: A Case of 
      Successful Bronchoscopic Retrieval.
PG  - e70787
LID - 10.1002/ccr3.70787 [doi]
LID - e70787
AB  - Foreign body aspiration in tracheostomized patients is preventable. This novel 
      case highlights the aspiration of a spectacle handle during stoma care-an 
      unreported hazard from repurposing nonmedical tools. Proactive education on 
      sterile techniques and avoiding household items is critical. Flexible 
      bronchoscopy proved effective despite altered anatomy postlaryngectomy.
