TI  - Artificial Intelligence in Interventional Pulmonology.
PG  - 29768675251353390
LID - 10.1177/29768675251353390 [doi]
LID - 29768675251353390
AB  - Artificial intelligence (AI) is an exciting new technology poised to drastically 
      improve the practice of medicine. Interventional pulmonology (IP) is particularly 
      well situated to implement AI due to the variety of complex diagnostic and 
      therapeutic techniques within its scope. By integrating AI into the field, the 
      procedure planning and management of pulmonary disease should become easier, more 
      accessible, and more effective. AI has already been implemented in the diagnostic 
      techniques of navigational and virtual bronchoscopy, endobronchial ultrasound, 
      and for the rapid onsite evaluation of pathological specimens. The goal of this 
      review is to summarize recent utilization of AI in IP and to discuss the origins 
      of the technology, ethical considerations, and future directions.
