TI  - Endoscopic Approaches to Central Airway Obstuction and Life-Threatening 
      Hemopytsis.
PG  - 299-308
LID - S1547-4127(25)00029-5 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.thorsurg.2025.05.002 [doi]
AB  - Central airway obstruction (CAO) is a critical condition characterized by the 
      blockage of the trachea or mainstem bronchi, leading to respiratory distress. 
      Diagnosis involves clinical assessment, pulmonary function tests, and imaging, 
      with flexible bronchoscopy being the gold standard for direct visualization and 
      intervention. Endoscopic techniques has revolutionized CAO management through 
      minimally invasive techniques such as endobronchial tumor debulking, airway 
      stenting, and balloon dilation. These methods aim to restore airway patency and 
      control bleeding, improving patient outcomes. This review article highlights the 
      importance of early recognition and the evolving therapeutic landscape in 
      managing these complex airway conditions.
