TI  - Treatment of Bronchopleural Fistula.
PG  - 383-391
LID - S0272-5231(25)00017-6 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.ccm.2025.02.015 [doi]
AB  - Bronchopleural fistula (BPF) is a challenging clinical condition characterized by 
      an abnormal connection between the bronchial tree and the pleural space. This 
      article aims to provide a thorough review of BPF, encompassing its etiologies, 
      clinical manifestations, diagnostic approaches, and treatment options. Current 
      advancements and future directions in BPF management will also be discussed.
