AB  - Bronchial aspergilloma, an uncommon subtype of pulmonary aspergilloma, likely 
      developed in the main bronchus due to airflow stagnation and dryness following 
      lobectomy. Detailed imaging and bronchoscopy provided valuable diagnostic 
      insights, underscoring the importance of considering fungal infections in 
      surgically altered airways.
