TI  - Downsizing Overlap Stenting for Bronchial Anastomotic Dehiscence Size Mismatch in 
      Lung Transplant.
PG  - e70116
LID - 10.1002/rcr2.70116 [doi]
LID - e70116
AB  - Bronchial dehiscence is a known complication following lung transplantation. In 
      cases involving extensive airway necrosis and air leaks, bronchoscopic placement 
      of self-expanding metallic stents provides an effective and safe management 
      strategy. These stents facilitate granulation and tissue reepithelialization. We 
      present a case of bronchial anastomotic dehiscence size mismatch after a lung 
      transplant. This complication was successfully managed using three stents placed 
      via a telescoping technique with flexible bronchoscopy.
