TI  - Endobronchial Lipoma Causing Almost Completely Trachea Obstruction.
PG  - e70112
LID - 10.1002/rcr2.70112 [doi]
LID - e70112
AB  - Even though endobronchial lipoma is rare, it can mimic malignancy and lead to 
      significant complications such as progressive dyspnea and subsequent lung 
      infections related to endobronchial obstruction. We present a case of 
      endobronchial lipoma located in the trachea causing almost complete tracheal 
      obstruction. The patient's dyspnea disappeared after undergoing bronchoscopic 
      excision of the mass.
