TI  - A Case of Thoracic SMARCA4-Deficient Undifferentiated Tumor on 18F-FDG PET/CT.
PG  - 170-172
LID - 10.1055/a-2383-2527 [doi]
AB  - A 65-year-old man, who denied a smoking history, presented with chest distress 
      and pain persisting for over a week. A contrast-enhanced chest CT scan revealed a 
      large irregular mass in the right thoracic cavity with heterogeneous enhancement. 
      The 18F-FDG PET/CT showed a large mass in the right thoracic cavity with 
      heterogeneous markedly high FDG uptake. The patient subsequently underwent a 
      bronchoscopic-guided mucosal biopsy at the opening of the right upper lobe. The 
      histological and immunohistochemical findings were consistent with thoracic 
      SMARCA4-deficient undifferentiated tumor.
