TI  - Pulmonary Artery Stent Molding Using a Rigid Bronchoscope: A Case Report.
PG  - 105397
LID - 10.1016/j.jscai.2026.105397 [doi]
LID - 105397
AB  - Bronchial compression following pulmonary artery endovascular stenting is a 
      well-reported phenomenon with significant impact on the course of care for 
      patients with congenital heart disease. There is a paucity of techniques 
      described to either prevent or address this postprocedural complication. We 
      report our successful experience with a novel technical variation-using a rigid 
      bronchoscope-to address postpulmonary artery stent airway compression in a 
      patient with single ventricle pathology.
