TI  - [Expert consensus on airway lavage therapy for adult burn patients (2026 
      edition)].
PG  - 403-414
LID - 10.3760/cma.j.cn501225-20260212-00080 [doi]
AB  - Airway lavage therapy is an important method for clearing airway secretions and 
      sloughed tissue in burn patients. It primarily includes fiberoptic 
      bronchoscopy-guided lavage and direct airway lavage. To further improve the 
      standardization, safety, and effectiveness of airway lavage therapy in burn 
      patients, the consensus writing group, based on evidence from evidence-based 
      medicine and guided by the Delphi method, conducted literature searches, quality 
      evaluations, evidence synthesis, and expert consultations. They formulated the 
      Expert consensus on airway lavage therapy for adult burn patients (2026 edition), 
      which provides a reference for clinical practice, covering topics such as 
      indications, contraindications, pre-operational preparation, timing and protocols 
      of operation, monitoring, and complication management of airway lavage therapy 
      for adult burn patients.
