PG  - 8374435
LID - 10.1155/crpu/8374435 [doi]
LID - 8374435
AB  - Foreign body aspiration among adults and older children could be more common than 
      previously documented. We present below eight cases of incidentally found airway 
      foreign bodies (FB) during endoscopic evaluation of patients performed due to 
      various indications such as chronic cough, nonresolving pneumonia and suspected 
      malignancy, among others. A high index of suspicion and prompt management are 
      required to prevent morbidity and complications associated with long-standing 
      airway FB.
