TI  - Bronchoscopic View and Treatment of a Nine-Year Slowly Enlarging Chronic Lung 
      Abscess Mimicking Lung Cancer.
PG  - e70552
LID - 10.1002/rcr2.70552 [doi]
LID - e70552
AB  - A 53-year-old male presented with a nine-year slowly enlarging cystic nodule. 
      Bronchoscopy visualised a protruding lesion, and a biopsy resulted in purulent 
      drainage. This case highlights that lung abscess can mimic lung cancer by 
      presenting as a slowly enlarging nodule and may be treatable using an ultra-thin 
      bronchoscope.
