TI  - A Case of Primary Endobronchial Hyalinizing Clear Cell Carcinoma Presenting as an 
      Oncologic Emergency Due to Complete Left Main Bronchus Obstruction Successfully 
      Managed with Airway Intervention.
LID - 10.2169/internalmedicine.7136-26 [doi]
AB  - A 66-year-old man presented with dyspnea and severe hypoxemia, requiring 
      mechanical ventilation. Computed tomography revealed an obstruction of the left 
      main bronchus by a bronchial tumor, thus prompting airway intervention to relieve 
      the stenosis. A histopathological examination of the tumor revealed clear 
      cytoplasm and hyalinized stroma, and rearrangement of EWSR1 was detected by a 
      fluorescence in situ hybridization analysis. Comprehensive genomic profiling was 
      performed because of the rarity of this case. GenMineTOP, capable of detecting 
      the EWSR1::ATF1 fusion, contributed to a definitive diagnosis of hyalinizing 
      clear cell carcinoma. Bronchoscopic airway intervention can serve as both a 
      therapeutic and diagnostic procedure; GenMineTOP was useful in establishing a 
      definitive diagnosis.
