TI  - Successful Removal of a Screw Nail From the Right Lower Lobe in a 1-Year-Old: New 
      Hybrid Technique: Case Report and Literature Review.
PG  - e71318
LID - 10.1002/ccr3.71318 [doi]
LID - e71318
AB  - Instantly, in the operating room, multidisciplinary critical thinking and 
      collaboration between pediatric ENT and pulmonology teams enabled the development 
      of an innovative hybrid technique for distal airway foreign body removal in a 
      challenging infant case. The approach combined flexible bronchoscopy for 
      visualization with malleable forceps through a rigid scope, providing a safe and 
      minimally invasive intervention in comparison to surgery.
