OAB - A 17-year-old girl fell from a 6-meter-high bridge, breaking her spine and heels. 
      Although her chest looked normal at first, she later developed serious breathing 
      problems. Doctors believe the strong impact from the fall caused hidden lung 
      damage through a “deceleration force”, a sudden stop that injured lung tissues 
      without breaking ribs. This led to a rare condition called ARDS. The case shows 
      that even without chest injury, dangerous lung problems can still happen after 
      big falls. Careful follow-up is important.
