TI  - Acute respiratory distress syndrome after administration of lidocaine in 
      bronchoscopy.
PG  - 197-200
LID - 10.4103/lungindia.lungindia_191_25 [doi]
AB  - Lidocaine is the most commonly used local anaesthetic agent for bronchoscopy, and 
      adverse reactions secondary to its use have rarely been reported. Among the 
      possible adverse reactions, the most common is lidocaine toxicity. Secondary 
      reactions to the use of nontoxic doses of lidocaine are infrequent, and acute 
      respiratory distress syndrome following its administration is exceptional.
