TI  - From Inception to Innovation: Journey of the Indian Academy of 
      Pediatrics-National Respiratory Chapter (IAP-NRC).
PG  - 133-136
LID - 10.1007/s13312-025-00256-6 [doi]
AB  - The Indian Academy of Pediatrics-National Respiratory Chapter (IAP-NRC) has 
      played a transformative role in shaping pediatric respiratory care in India. 
      Since its inception in 1989, it has evolved from a focused platform dedicated to 
      childhood respiratory disorders to a nationally recognized academic body driving 
      excellence in pediatric pulmonology. To bring uniformity and quality to 
      respiratory care, it has created a robust ecosystem of education, collaborative 
      learning and capacity-building through its nationwide activities like structured 
      training programs, including asthma training modules (ATM), basic as well as 
      advanced pediatric bronchoscopy courses, basic pediatric pulmonology master 
      classes, pediatric pulmonology fellowship programs, evidence-based protocols, 
      advocacy activities, and development of various national guidelines. The Journal 
      of Pediatric Pulmonology, a quarterly publication of IAP-NRC, is dedicated to 
      nurturing young pediatricians in research and promoting the generation of new 
      evidence in pediatric pulmonology. The chapter's next strategic goal is to 
      integrate digital health innovations and strengthen global collaborations to 
      address emerging respiratory challenges. Together, these initiatives reflect 
      IAP-NRC's steadfast commitment to improving respiratory health for every child in 
      India.
