TI  - [A case report of tracheobronchial Dieulafoy's disease].
PG  - 860-862
LID - 10.3760/cma.j.cn112147-20250706-00381 [doi]
AB  - Tracheobronchial Dieulafoy's disease (TBDD) is a rare bronchial artery vascular 
      malformation, characterized clinically by sudden, recurrent, and life-threatening 
      massive hemoptysis. This article reports the case of a 9-year-old female patient 
      who presented with massive hemoptysis lasting two weeks. Following ineffective 
      treatment at a local hospital, she was transferred to our institution. 
      Bronchoscopy revealed a smooth, submucosal protrusion at the orifice of the right 
      lower lobe basal segment. Digital subtraction angiography (DSA) revealed tortuous 
      bronchial arteries near the lesion, indicating a caliber-persistent artery 
      malformation. Following embolization with Onyx, the patient's hemoptysis 
      resolved, and follow-up bronchoscopy confirmed the disappearance of the lesion.
