TI  - Endobronchial Leiomyoma Presenting as Post-Obstructive Pneumonia.
PG  - e70124
LID - 10.1002/rcr2.70124 [doi]
LID - e70124
AB  - Endobronchial leiomyoma is a rare airway tumour. We report the case of a 
      30-year-old female non-smoker who presented with persistent fever and cough, 
      ultimately diagnosed with post-obstructive pneumonia secondary to an 
      endobronchial leiomyoma. The patient underwent a successful endobronchial 
      cryo-resection with the resolution of symptoms. This case highlights the 
      importance of considering rare causes of non-resolving pneumonia and the role of 
      a minimally invasive approach in the management of endobronchial leiomyoma.
