DP  - 2025 Feb
TI  - A Case of Non-Anastomotic Tracheo-Thoracic Gastric Fistula.
PG  - e70096
LID - 10.1002/rcr2.70096 [doi]
LID - e70096
AB  - Tracheo-thoracic gastric fistula (TTGF) is a rare but serious complication 
      following oesophageal cancer surgery, involving an abnormal connection between 
      the thoracic gastric cavity and the bronchial tree. We report a case of TTGF that 
      developed 3 years post-esophagectomy, identified through bronchoscopy. The 
      patient was treated using a multidisciplinary approach, which included the 
      placement of a bronchial covered stent, insertion of a jejunostomy feeding tube, 
      and gastrointestinal decompression. The intervention resulted in a marked 
      improvement in the patient's respiratory distress and fever, leading to a 
      successful discharge. This case highlights the necessity for individualised 
      treatment strategies for TTGF and underscores the crucial role of 
      multidisciplinary management in enhancing patient outcomes.
