TI  - A 30-year-old male with innumerable millimetric pulmonary nodules: tunnelling 
      thoughts.
PG  - 102461
LID - 10.1016/j.rmcr.2026.102461 [doi]
LID - 102461
AB  - We report the case of a young Syrian male who presented to the emergency ward 
      with mild exertional dyspnea and centrilobular millimetric pulmonary nodules. 
      Given the broad differential and inconclusive medical history, a comprehensive 
      diagnostic work-up was undertaken. Bronchoscopy with lymph node biopsy revealed a 
      non-specific granuloma, while concurrent infectious screening identified 
      tuberculosis infection (TBI). Further assessment of his occupational history 
      revealed tunnelling work and raised a clinical suspicion for silicosis, an 
      interstitial lung disease caused by the inhalation of crystalline silica dust, 
      which was confirmed by pulmonary biopsy.
