TI  - Aspiration Pneumonia and Difficult Removal of an Exfoliated Primary Tooth-A Case 
      Report.
PG  - e72300
LID - 10.1002/ccr3.72300 [doi]
LID - e72300
AB  - The aspiration of exfoliated primary teeth is extremely rare yet presents a high 
      risk for aspiration pneumonia. This is the first reported case in a child with no 
      underlying conditions. Expertise in the removal of foreign bodies is vital for an 
      optimal treatment outcome and should be performed at specialist centers.
