      Endobronchial Involvement.
PG  - e70486
LID - 10.1002/rcr2.70486 [doi]
LID - e70486
AB  - A 74-year-old man with prior stage IE gastric MALT lymphoma presented with 
      blood-stained sputum. Autofluorescence imaging (AFI) bronchoscopy revealed 
      bilateral endobronchial lesions; with biopsies confirmed MALT lymphoma. Positron 
      emission tomography computed tomography showed right upper lobe lesion without 
      nodal disease. He received rituximab, with complete metabolic response. AFI 
      facilitated early airway-focused diagnosis.
