TI  - A Young Man With Primary Pulmonary Myxoma.
PG  - e70815
LID - 10.1002/ccr3.70815 [doi]
LID - e70815
AB  - Primary pulmonary myxoma is a rare tumor and is usually diagnosed incidentally in 
      clinically asymptomatic patients as a well-defined lung mass without 
      metastasizing. It should also be considered that diagnostic methods such as 
      bronchoscopy or transthoracic aspiration may be nondiagnostic. Thus, tumor 
      resection is essential for diagnosis and treatment.
