TI  - FDG PET/CT in a Case of Tracheal Inflammatory Myofibroblastic Tumor.
PG  - e177-e178
LID - 10.1097/RLU.0000000000006084 [doi]
AB  - Tracheal inflammatory myofibroblastic tumors are exceedingly uncommon. This 
      report presents the findings from an FDG PET/CT scan in a case involving an 
      intratracheal inflammatory myofibroblastic tumor. Bronchoscopy revealed a 
      neoplastic growth on the left lateral wall of the mid-trachea. The subsequent FDG 
      PET/CT scan demonstrated intense radiotracer uptake within the lesion, with a 
      maximum standardized uptake value (SUVmax) of 8.0. Post-surgical resection, 
      immunohistochemical analysis corroborated the diagnosis of a tracheal 
      inflammatory myofibroblastic tumor.
