AB  - We report a case of bronchial Dieulafoy presenting with haemoptysis, initially 
      resembling an endobronchial tumour on bronchoscopy. This case highlights the 
      critical role of EBUS in the assessment of suspicious endobronchial lesions and 
      in preventing potentially life-threatening complications from inadvertent biopsy.
