TI  - Diagnosis of the Solitary Pulmonary Nodule.
PG  - 271-288
LID - S0272-5231(25)00008-5 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.ccm.2025.02.006 [doi]
AB  - Approximately 1.6 million people in the United States alone are diagnosed 
      annually with a pulmonary nodule. Clinicians are tasked with determining the 
      etiology and assessing which nodule may represent cancer. Nodule calculators use 
      patient demographics and nodule characteristics to assess the likelihood of 
      cancer, and biomarkers may improve risk assessment. Appropriate risk 
      stratification and adherence to guideline-concordant management limits 
      unnecessary invasive testing. When tissue acquisition is necessary, the clinician 
      should understand the risks and benefits of various diagnostic modalities.
