TI  - Kartagener syndrome combined with small cell lung cancer: A case report and 
      literature review.
PG  - 98
LID - 10.3892/etm.2025.12848 [doi]
LID - 98
AB  - Kartagener syndrome (KS) is a rare autosomal recessive genetic disease 
      characterized by visceral inversion, sinusitis and bronchiectasis. Small-cell 
      lung cancer, a common tumor with poor prognosis, rarely coexists with KS. The 
      lack of typical clinical symptoms can lead to missed or incorrect diagnoses, and 
      to date, only few cases of this combination have been reported. The current study 
      presents a case of KS with small cell lung cancer that was promptly diagnosed and 
      treated at Jining No. 1 People's Hospital (Jining, China). Sharing this case may 
      contribute to the advancement of respiratory medicine and aid doctors in the 
      diagnosis and management of similar conditions.
