TI  - Squamous cell carcinoma of the bronchus associated with human papillomavirus 
      infection.
PG  - 102162
LID - 10.1016/j.rmcr.2024.102162 [doi]
LID - 102162
AB  - A woman in her 70s presented with an abnormal chest radiograph. Chest computed 
      tomography showed a tumor arising from the intermediate bronchus. A bronchoscopic 
      biopsy revealed squamous cell carcinoma, and right middle and lower bilobectomy 
      was subsequently carried out. Histopathological examination of the resected 
      specimen revealed squamous cell carcinoma associated with human papillomavirus 
      infection.
